entries.english:
Adam Friedrich [von Seinsheim], Bischof zu Würzburg, grants the following properties as male fiefs to Johann Philipp, canon of Würzburg, and Adalbert Friedrich, episcopal councillor and Amtmann at Arnstein, sons of the late episcopal councillor and Amtmann at Grünsfeld, Anton Philibert von Rosenbach:
- Thundorf Castle with all rights, appurtenances, and revenues, except only the farmyard;
- the deserted settlement of Ransbach (Ramspach), with its mill and farm and all rights and revenues;
- the villages of Theinfeld and Rothhausen, with all rights, holdings, and revenues there;
- an estate at Maßbach behind the churchyard;
- the estates at Poppenlauer;
- the estates at Ebertshausen;
- half the tithe at Altenmünster (Münster auf dem Schlattach);
- one third of the tithe at Oberlauringen;
- one eighth of the tithe at Alsleben;
- one quarter of the tithe at Ober- and Untereßfeld;
- a vineyard and two woods at Thundorf.

The Bischof further grants them the following properties, which Veit Ulrich von Schaumberg had held as allodial property and then enfeoffed to the Hochstift Würzburg:
- the farmyard and vineyards at Thundorf;
- the lake at Weißensee;
- a fishing right in the Lauer below Maßbach;
- a fishing right in the Lauer within the Rothhausen district;
- three quarters of the mill at Rothhausen;
- two estates at Theinfeld;
- two freehold estates at Weichtungen;
- four rent fiefs at Stadtlauringen;
- nine estates and eleven fiefs at Maßbach;
- the Brandmühle below Maßbach;
- five estates and four fiefs at Poppenlauer;
- three estates and one fief at Nüdlingen;
- one fief at Rannungen;
- a field estate at Hesselbach;
- the Herlingsberg wood;
- the male fief at Prappach.
These properties were purchased from the brothers Georg Dietrich, Wilhelm Ludwig, Wilhelm Ulrich, Georg Wilhelm, Johann Sigmund, Johann Philipp, and Johann Wilhelm von Schaumberg.

Finally, the Bischof also grants them the following properties, originally held in fief from the County of Henneberg and then from the Duchy of Saxe-Weimar, which passed to Würzburg under an agreement between the Hochstift Würzburg and the Duchy of Saxe-Weimar:
- the cent court at Maßbach, subsequently transferred to Poppenlauer, with all appurtenances and rights, excluding the villages of Maßbach and Volkershausen;
- half the Vogtei at Poppenlauer;
- two estates at Maßbach and a meadow between Maßbach and Rothhausen;
- one quarter of the tithe at Zeil am Main;
- one third of a small quarter of the wine tithe at Zeil am Main;
- one third and one quarter of a full quarter of the wine tithe at Zeil am Main;
- four woods near Maßbach;
- the wine rents and rent revenues at Schonungen. If the von Rosenbach family should ever have no male heirs, the Hochstift Würzburg is obliged to pay the family’s female heirs 2,000 Reichstaler in compensation for the reversion of these revenues.

Sealer: the Bischof, with his private seal.

Notes: Abstract (18th century).
